         <div class="tl-logo"><img src="{{ '/assets/img/logos/epsilla.png' | relative_url }}" alt="Epsilla"></div> -->
    <div class="tl-logo"></div>
    <div class="tl-body">
      <p class="tl-role">AI Engineer</p>
      <p class="tl-company"><a href="https://www.epsilla.com" target="_blank">Epsilla (YC S23)</a> · Internship</p>
      <p class="tl-meta">Feb 2026 - Present · Remote</p>
      <p class="tl-proj">Shipped <strong>Stanford SIS</strong> end-to-end as a Next.js product over three backends: a biomedical knowledge graph in <strong>Google Spanner</strong> with 2.5M+ articles, Neon Postgres for all product state, and the Epsilla RAG agent runtime. Exposed the graph to cloud agents through <strong>MCP servers</strong> with a subgraph cache, and built embedding-based alert subscriptions that match user queries against newly ingested claims. Built gene monograph generation on the same graph, assembling ranked claims with evidence strength into an evidence package shared by the writer model and the MCP tools, persisted as append-only versions so prior links never break.</p>
      <p class="tl-proj">Co-authored and released <a href="https://github.com/epsilla-cloud/clawtrace" target="_blank"><strong>ClawTrace</strong></a>, an open-source <strong>cost-aware tracing platform</strong> for LLM agents. Captures LLM calls, tool calls, and sub-agent spans into a streaming pipeline that lands events in a cloud data lake and exposes them as a queryable graph, giving per-step cost and token attribution across 80+ models, with an AI analyst that diagnoses expensive runs and a skill-distillation layer that turns traces into reusable agent instructions.</p>
      <p class="tl-proj">Built the shared <strong>identity and authorization core</strong> every Epsilla product signs in through - stateless org-scoped JWTs, Google sign-in, and idempotent onboarding workflows over a graph-backed multi-tenant store - and worked on <strong>HarnessRouter</strong>, an OpenAI-compatible API that runs coding agents in isolated sandboxes and returns finished artifacts.</p>
      <p class="tl-pubs-label">Publications</p>
      <ul class="tl-pubs">
        <li><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.23853" target="_blank">ClawTrace: Cost-Aware Tracing for LLM Agent Skill Distillation</a> <span class="tl-venue">· ACM CAIS 2026 Workshop on Agent Skills (Oral)</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="tl-item">
    <div class="tl-date">2024</div>
    <div class="tl-rail"><span class="tl-dot"></span></div>
    <div class="tl-logo"></div>
    <div class="tl-body">
      <p class="tl-role">Software Engineer Intern</p>
      <p class="tl-company">Meituan · Internship</p>
      <p class="tl-meta">Jun 2024 - Aug 2024 · Shenzhen, China</p>
      <p class="tl-desc">Built a scalable Python microservice for <strong>batch PDF processing</strong> in production, handling ingestion, processing, and delivery through an API and parallelizing work at the page level so large documents process independently and failures stay isolated. Made the pipeline <strong>layout-aware</strong> rather than OCR-only: <strong>PyMuPDF</strong> parses text, images, and layout while a <strong>Detectron2</strong> model detects document structure - titles, paragraphs, tables, figures - and OCR runs selectively where no text is recoverable, improving extraction accuracy 22% over text-only parsing. Fused text with detected structure into a machine-readable representation of typed blocks with coordinates, so downstream search and extraction work from structured JSON. Containerized with <strong>Docker</strong> and deployed on <strong>Kubernetes</strong> with horizontal scaling and rolling updates, cutting end-to-end latency 40% with zero-downtime releases.</p>
